#: src/sshpilot/connection_dialog.py:3944
msgid ""
"Port forwarding allows you to securely tunnel network connections.\n"
"\n"
"• <b>Local Forwarding</b>: A port on the local machine is forwarded to the "
"specified host and port from the remote machine.\n"
"• <b>Remote Forwarding</b>: A port on the remote machine is forwarded to a "
"specified host and port from the local machine.\n"
"• <b>Dynamic Forwarding</b>: Starts a SOCKS proxy on the local machine "
"listening on the specified port."
msgstr ""
"El reenvío de puertos le permite tunelizar conexiones de red de forma "
"segura.\n"
"\n"
"• <b>Reenvío local</b>: Un puerto de la máquina local se reenvía al host y "
"puerto especificados desde la máquina remota.\n"
"• <b>Reenvío remoto</b>: Un puerto de la máquina remota se reenvía a un host "
"y puerto especificados desde la máquina local.\n"
"• <b>Reenvío dinámico</b>: Inicia un proxy SOCKS en la máquina local "
"escuchando en el puerto especificado."

#: src/sshpilot/connection_dialog.py:3963
msgid "Opens the way to the host before SSH Pilot connects. Choose one."
msgstr ""
"Abre el acceso al host antes de que SSH Pilot se conecte. Elija una opción."

#: src/sshpilot/connection_dialog.py:3968
msgid "Runs before SSH Pilot connects, for example to bring up a VPN."
msgstr ""

#: src/sshpilot/connection_dialog.py:3973
msgid ""
"Ports to reach for, in order, such as 7000,8000,9000. Add :udp to a port for "
"UDP. Sent by SSH Pilot itself, so no knock tool has to be installed."
msgstr ""
"Puertos a contactar, en orden, como 7000,8000,9000. Añada :udp a un puerto "
"para UDP. Enviados directamente por SSH Pilot, por lo que no es necesario "
"instalar ninguna herramienta de knock."

#: src/sshpilot/connection_dialog.py:3978
msgid ""
"Anything else that has to run first — fwknop, a VPN dial-up, or a knock and "
"a VPN together in one line."
msgstr ""
"Cualquier otra cosa que deba ejecutarse primero: fwknop, una conexión VPN o "
"un knock y una VPN juntos en una sola línea."

#: src/sshpilot/connection_dialog.py:3982
msgid ""
"Sent to OpenSSH.\n"
"\n"
"• Local Command: runs on your machine after connecting (requires "
"PermitLocalCommand).\n"
"• Remote Command: runs on the host (RequestTTY is configured separately)."
msgstr ""
"Enviado a OpenSSH.\n"
"\n"
"• Comando local: se ejecuta en su equipo después de conectarse (requiere "
"PermitLocalCommand).\n"
"• Comando remoto: se ejecuta en el host (RequestTTY se configura por "
"separado)."

